WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.294
Journey two: view a business and its products.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.139
Here is what the app does now.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:14.849
When an owner sets a product’s stock to zero, a toast says it is sold out,

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:18.172
and that members can still ask to be told when it’s back.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:24.089
On the shop page, the card of that product says: Sold out.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.758
In words, on a desktop and on a phone.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:34.155
On the product page, a member presses: Tell me when it’s back.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.966
The page answers: We’ll tell you when it’s back.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:44.655
When the stock returns, each member who asked is notified once:

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:49.055
a toast with View in shop, and a line in their notifications.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:54.520
They get one e-mail too, unless they turned Request updates off.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:59.699
Jubilee takes no payment. The shop confirms stock and says how to pay.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:05.300
An owner who opens a listing that is not public sees a preview, with its status.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:07.224
So does the verification team.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:16.600
Jubilee helps Christian business owners in Toronto do well in business and use what they earn to support God’s work.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:20.049
We do this because we love Jesus and stay close to Him.
